It shall be unlawful for any person to maintain or keep in such a manner or in such conditions that it is a public nuisance or otherwise allow an animal owned or maintained by such a person to act so as to constitute a public nuisance animal. Any animal will be deemed a public nuisance animal if such animal:
(1) Is repeatedly found at-large;
(2) Damages, soils, eliminates, or defecates on private property other than its owner's property or public property;
(3) Causes unsanitary or offensive conditions or otherwise endangers public health, welfare or safety;
(4) Chases vehicles, bicycles, or people;
(5) Is in estrus/heat and not confined in a manner which can keep it away from intact males of the same species;
(6) Causes damages, defilement, or death of another domesticated animal on private property other than its owners' property or on public property;
(7) Is found to be a biting or attaching animal;
(8) It shall be unlawful for any owner to allow to allow any animal to cause a disturbance by barking, howling, or other noisemaking for either (a) continuously for a period of at least 30 minutes; or (b) intermittently for a period of at least one (1) hour. No citation for violation of this subsection shall be issued unless there are at least two complaining witnesses from different residences who shall have signed a written statement stating the address of the dog owner, a description of the dog and of the offense and the date, time, and location of the offense or one complaining witness who shall have signed a written statement stating the address of the dog owner, a description of the dog and of the offense and the date, time and location of the offense and some form of audio and or video recording of the offense.
(9) Is any feline that is allowed to roam off of its owner's property unless such feline is spayed or neutered.
(Ord. of 3-27-2018, § 1(Exh. A))

